code,core,ui: split long functions instead of allowing too_many_lines

Pedantic clippy flagged four functions over the 100-line limit. Each
had clear seams at the role/phase boundaries, so extract helpers
(bash's host-command constructor and race-outcome mapping, exec's CPU
guard installer, to_openai_chat_messages per-role emitters, the
compaction-restore test's seed helpers) rather than ship allow
attributes the codebase otherwise avoids.

While the lint door was open, fix the remaining pedantic items:
doc backticks on QuickJS and a quoted error message,
ExecCtx::Debug::finish_non_exhaustive since closures are intentionally
omitted, writeln! over format!+push_str, and two let mut that did not
need mut.